(12288, 'GwennenGossipTujen', '[]', 'We''ve campaigned together for many years. It''s taken a great toll on him, but he soldiers on. I don''t know how he remains so cheery, honestly. If he loses another limb, he''ll be more metal than man...', 'Audio/Dialogue/NPC/Gwennen/Gwennen_86.ogg', '', 0, 0, '', 1, 0, 1, '[512,520,516]', NULL, 0, 0, '[]', 100),
(12289, 'GwennenGossipRog', '[]', 'He''s a sweetheart. Have you seen the figurines he carves? The four of us use them to play this delightfully strange game he came up with. I love it because there are so many dice rolls, and, well, you know me.', 'Audio/Dialogue/NPC/Gwennen/Gwennen_87.ogg', '', 0, 0, '', 1, 0, 1, '[512,520,516]', NULL, 0, 0, '[]', 100),
(12290, 'GwennenGossipDannig', '[]', 'Our intrepid leader believes in a world better than the one that truly is. He doesn''t see you and me, Exile. He sees heroes. He sees grandiose myths and world-changing bravery. Don''t dispel those notions. I want to live in the world he sees, even if I know it isn''t real.', 'Audio/Dialogue/NPC/Gwennen/Gwennen_88.ogg', '', 0, 0, '', 1, 0, 1, '[512,520,516]', NULL, 0, 0, '[]', 100),
(12291, 'GwennenGossipLuckOne', '[]', 'During the failed rebellion, I once called out with all my heart. An arrow was arcing through the air. My arm was pinned, and I knew I couldn''t get out of the way in time. I was a dead woman. But Luck answered my earnest request. Another arrow, also on a murderous path, hit the first <i>{in midair}, and both were diverted, landing on either side of me instead! That was the first time I knew that Chance itself was a real force in this world.', 'Audio/Dialogue/NPC/Gwennen/Gwennen_89.ogg', '', 0, 0, '', 1, 0, 1, '[512,520,516]', NULL, 0, 0, '[]', 100),
(12292, 'GwennenGossipFailedRebellion', '[]', 'I didn''t say that. You must have misheard.', 'Audio/Dialogue/NPC/Gwennen/Gwennen_90.ogg', '', 0, 0, '', 1, 0, 1, '[512,520,516]', NULL, 0, 0, '[]', 100),
(12293, 'GwennenGossipLuckTwo', '[]', 'During... an unspecified war... I once called out with all my heart. An arrow was arcing through the air. My arm was pinned, and I knew I couldn''t get out of the way in time. I was a dead woman. But Luck answered my earnest request. Another arrow, also on a murderous path, hit the first <i>{in midair}, and both were diverted, landing on either side of me instead! That was the first time I knew that Chance itself was a real force in this world.', 'Audio/Dialogue/NPC/Gwennen/Gwennen_91.ogg', '', 0, 0, '', 1, 0, 1, '[512,520,516]', NULL, 0, 0, '[]', 100),
(12294, 'GwennenGossipTheKing', '[]', 'You''re pushing your luck with questions like that, Exile. Don''t waste it. You''ll need every scrap of fortune you can get when the time comes.', 'Audio/Dialogue/NPC/Gwennen/Gwennen_92.ogg', '', 0, 0, '', 1, 0, 1, '[512,520,516]', NULL, 0, 0, '[]', 100),
(12295, 'GwennenGossipGods', '[]', 'Never heard of ''gods,'' but I know I wouldn''t put my faith in them even if they came to my doorstep with an army. I''ve already solidified my beliefs where they belong.', 'Audio/Dialogue/NPC/Gwennen/Gwennen_93.ogg', '', 0, 0, '', 1, 0, 1, '[512,520,516]', NULL, 0, 0, '[]', 100),
(12296, 'GwennenGossipDruidsOfTheBrokenCircle', '[]', 'I am honour-bound to discover the fate of Medved and the Druids of the Broken Circle. They believed they could see into the future by peering into the past. Hypothetically, that''s a power I''d very much like to have, for reasons of chance and profit... but I''m not sure I want it to be true. If Medved and his nature-mystics were right and Time truly is a circle, aren''t we all doomed to repeat our lives over and over for eternity? If that is the truth, then there is no luck. No chance, no human will. All life is just a stageplay repeating over and over. I don''t think I like that notion.', 'Audio/Dialogue/NPC/Gwennen/Gwennen_94.ogg', '', 0, 0, '', 1, 0, 1, '[512,520,516]', NULL, 0, 0, '[]', 100),
(12297, 'GwennenGossipMedved', '[]', 'His final fate was unknown, but I do know he cast off his peaceful ways and trained with two powerful axes after he arrived here. We''re not fools. We see that the dead rise here on Wraeclast. If Medved is still out there, he''ll be extremely dangerous. Conserve your luck, and use it against him if you find him.', 'Audio/Dialogue/NPC/Gwennen/Gwennen_95.ogg', '', 0, 0, '', 1, 0, 1, '[512,520,516]', NULL, 0, 0, '[]', 100),
(12298, 'GwennenGossipMedvedStoryFound', '[]', 'So the Druids lost the ability to see into the past after Olroth began using Wraeclast''s forbidden gems... how strange... and Medved headed off into the dark of night to challenge the leader of the creatures to a one-on-one battle, no doubt. Honourable, but foolish. There''s more to this story, Exile. I hope you can find it.', 'Audio/Dialogue/NPC/Gwennen/Gwennen_96.ogg', '', 0, 0, '', 1, 0, 1, '[512,520,516]', NULL, 0, 0, '[]', 100),
(12299, 'GwennenGossipMedvedDefeatedStoryNotComplete', '[]', 'You have put Medved to rest after all this time. Thank you. I am descended from Annest, the daughter that he sent away before the end, so I could never leave here without ensuring my ancestor''s peace. That is one more step toward freedom.', 'Audio/Dialogue/NPC/Gwennen/Gwennen_97.ogg', '', 0, 0, '', 1, 0, 1, '[512,520,516]', NULL, 0, 0, '[]', 100),
(12300, 'GwennenGossipMedvedDefeatedStoryComplete', '[]', 'The tale is now complete. Medved was a noble and well-intentioned hero, but the darkness of Wraeclast corrupted him and turned him toward madness. Now that he has been put to rest, I am free. Once we find the Triskelion Flame, I can return home.' || char(13) || '
' || char(13) || '
I must thank you for this. I am descended from Annest, the daughter that Medved sent away before the end, so his actions mark the honour of my lineage. When we return home, I will end the tale at his journey into the night to challenge evil''s unseen leader. The Kalguur will know that he died in combat trying to save his people. The rest does not need to be told.', 'Audio/Dialogue/NPC/Gwennen/Gwennen_98.ogg', '', 0, 0, '', 1, 0, 1, '[512,520,516]', NULL, 0, 0, '[]', 100),
(12301, 'TujenIntroGeneralWitch', '[1]', 'The name''s Tujen. You''ve quite the aura of darkness. Glad to work with ya. That''s just the kind of temperament this Wraeclast demands.', 'Audio/Dialogue/NPC/Tujen/Tujen_02.ogg', '', 0, 0, '', 1, 0, 1, '[513,517,521]', NULL, 0, 0, '[]', 100),
(12302, 'TujenIntroGeneralScion', '[2]', 'The name''s Tujen. You''re to do the dirty work while we do the diggin''. It''s as good an alliance as any. Well, let''s hop to it.', 'Audio/Dialogue/NPC/Tujen/Tujen_01.ogg', '', 0, 0, '', 1, 0, 1, '[513,517,521]', NULL, 0, 0, '[]', 100),
(12303, 'TujenIntroGeneralRanger', '[3]', 'The name''s Tujen. You''re to do the dirty work while we do the diggin''. It''s as good an alliance as any. Well, let''s hop to it.', 'Audio/Dialogue/NPC/Tujen/Tujen_01.ogg', '', 0, 0, '', 1, 0, 1, '[513,517,521]', NULL, 0, 0, '[]', 100),
(12304, 'TujenIntroGeneralDuelist', '[4]', 'The name''s Tujen. You''re to do the dirty work while we do the diggin''. It''s as good an alliance as any. Well, let''s hop to it.', 'Audio/Dialogue/NPC/Tujen/Tujen_01.ogg', '', 0, 0, '', 1, 0, 1, '[513,517,521]', NULL, 0, 0, '[]', 100),
(12305, 'TujenIntroGeneralShadow', '[5]', 'Name''s Tujen. You''ve as murderous an edge as I''ve ever seen, though you hide it with a pleasant smile. Normally, I''d stay far away from one such as you, but this Wraeclast demands a bit of darkness. We''ll get on just fine.', 'Audio/Dialogue/NPC/Tujen/Tujen_03.ogg', '', 0, 0, '', 1, 0, 1, '[513,517,521]', NULL, 0, 0, '[]', 100),
(12306, 'TujenIntroGeneralTemplar', '[6]', 'The name''s Tujen. You''re to do the dirty work while we do the diggin''. It''s as good an alliance as any. Well, let''s hop to it.', 'Audio/Dialogue/NPC/Tujen/Tujen_01.ogg', '', 0, 0, '', 1, 0, 1, '[513,517,521]', NULL, 0, 0, '[]', 100),
(12307, 'TujenIntroMarauder', '[0]', 'The name''s Tujen. You''re to do the dirty work while we do the diggin''. It''s as good an alliance as any. Well, let''s hop to it.', 'Audio/Dialogue/NPC/Tujen/Tujen_01.ogg', '', 0, 0, '', 1, 0, 1, '[513,517,521]', NULL, 0, 0, '[]', 100),
