(25378, 'Varashta_FarewellCallout_11', '[]', 'The battle begins.', 'Audio/Dialogue/Leagues/Mirage/Varashta_Wild/Varashta_FarewellCallout_04_02.ogg', '', 0, 0, '', 1, 0, 1, '[788]', NULL, 0, 0, '[]', 100),
(25379, 'Varashta_FarewellCallout_12', '[]', 'The battle begins!', 'Audio/Dialogue/Leagues/Mirage/Varashta_Wild/Varashta_FarewellCallout_04_03.ogg', '', 0, 0, '', 1, 0, 1, '[788]', NULL, 0, 0, '[]', 100),
(25380, 'Varashta_OnSaresh', '[]', 'Ah, so the Afarud''s secret leader is Saresh, the Necromancer of Weeping Black! I was already bound to the Trial of the Sekhemas by his era. I know only what aspirants and <i>{djinn} have told me.' || char(13) || '
' || char(13) || '
He was a Walker of the White Sands, rejected even by the Faridun, though I know not why. Ahkeli''s Order found him, recruited him, and put his unique talents to work... but even they could not stomach his... <i>{interests}. Eventually, they banished him, and he sought refuge in a desert region. He became a Necromancer and built an army of the dead, and eventually waged war on us. Orbala was crowned Garukhan for uniting the <i>{akharas} and defeating him. The Afarud must have stolen him away after... perhaps Orbala''s victory was not complete...', 'Audio/Dialogue/Leagues/Mirage/Varashta/Varashta_OnSareshOne.ogg', '', 0, 0, '', 1, 0, 1, '[788]', NULL, 0, 0, '[]', 100),
(25381, 'Varashta_OnSareshTwo', '[]', 'You have won a great victory, but I am still concerned. Saresh was partly a <i>{djinn}, and partly undead? This is... impossible... the ritual of binding cannot be enacted on living flesh. It must be something like a coin, a sword, or a painting... unless... yes...that must be it. His undead body <i>{isn''t} a living thing, so the ritual must still work. How does one kill that which cannot die?' || char(13) || '
' || char(13) || '
He will return... I have no doubt...', 'Audio/Dialogue/Leagues/Mirage/Varashta/Varashta_OnSareshTwo.ogg', '', 0, 0, '', 1, 0, 1, '[788]', NULL, 0, 0, '[]', 100),
(25382, 'Varashta_OnWinterSekhema', '[]', 'Do they still call me the Winter Sekhema? I am always surprised at the lasting memory of my people. We survived the Winter of the World so long ago that the Vastiri has endured two or three entire eras since. There was a time of warming, of rains, of lush rivers and forests... then the slow growth of the sands and the salt flats... the passing of my beloved mastodons... and now the deserts, too, begin to change. It is subtle, and visible only to one who watches, like me, but I feel it in the air. Though it may take another thousand years, the rains will return. This is my wisdom for you: if you wait long enough, all things change.', 'Audio/Dialogue/Leagues/Mirage/Varashta/Varashta_OnWinterSekhema.ogg', '', 0, 0, '', 1, 0, 1, '[788]', NULL, 0, 0, '[]', 100),
(25383, 'Varashta_OnWinterOfTheWorld', '[]', 'You would not believe it now, but the Vastiri was once a land of snow, ice, and eternal gloom. We were a people clad completely in pale furs, meant to keep us warm and blend in with the snow. Kulemak himself once gazed directly at me, but led his army past. He had no idea I was kneeling there in the drift, glaring right back at him. I would have given my life to leap out and slit his rotting throat... but he''d have just risen from another body. Cowardly <i>{ji-tat!} ', 'Audio/Dialogue/Leagues/Mirage/Varashta/Varashta_OnWinterOfTheWorld.ogg', '', 0, 0, '', 1, 0, 1, '[788]', NULL, 0, 0, '[]', 100),
(25384, 'Varashta_OnKulemak', '[]', 'I''m not certain what happened. Last I heard about it, some sort of alliance had a plan to confront Kulemak. That was... some time ago... I''m not sure how long. I''m sure you would not be here if it had failed, so there is that.', 'Audio/Dialogue/Leagues/Mirage/Varashta/Varashta_OnKulemak.ogg', '', 0, 0, '', 1, 0, 1, '[788]', NULL, 0, 0, '[]', 100),
(25385, 'Varashta_OnDjinn', '[]', 'After returning from a journey to the islands of the south, and learning from the <i>{hatungo} there, I created the basis for what you now know as <i>{djinn}. My daughter, Rashi, was the first... though I have not seen her since she founded the <i>{sel khari}... she chose to do this. Those that agree to the ritual know far less pain. My people have long sentenced criminals to a time as <i>{djinn}.... these are the minor <i>{djinn} the Afarud wish to torture and exploit. Criminals, yes, but they''re <i>{our} criminals.', 'Audio/Dialogue/Leagues/Mirage/Varashta/Varashta_On_Djinn.ogg', '', 0, 0, '', 1, 0, 1, '[788]', NULL, 0, 0, '[]', 100),
(25386, 'Varashta_OnSentencedCriminals', '[]', 'I created the binding ritual to improve our lives, to give those who wished to serve the chance to aid future generations. I am still saddened by how quickly it became a tool of punishment, even in my own eyes. It was I who first sentenced criminals... traitors and fools in my own <i>{akhara}. Navira, Ruzhan, Kelari... I regret ever walking that path. I would take it back, if I could, but it''s too late for that.', 'Audio/Dialogue/Leagues/Mirage/Varashta/Varashta_OnSentencedCriminals.ogg', '', 0, 0, '', 1, 0, 1, '[788]', NULL, 0, 0, '[]', 100),
(25387, 'Varashta_VastiriDesertWild', '[]', 'The Vastiri! Seeing my home once again renews my determination...', 'Audio/Dialogue/Leagues/Mirage/Varashta_Wild/Varashta_VastiriDesertWild.ogg', '', 0, 0, '', 1, 0, 1, '[788]', NULL, 0, 0, '[]', 100),
(25388, 'Varashta_OnMirages', '[]', 'From what I observed, Zarokh is trying to... how do I explain this? If Time is a river, he is hooking his chains into it, and trying to pull it down another path... a path in which he was never bound in a <i>{barya}, perhaps. If he can exert enough force, chain enough of our history, he may succeed... but, until then, his Mirages are not real. They are pale shadows of the land and the creatures within... but not the people.', 'Audio/Dialogue/Leagues/Mirage/Varashta/Varashta_OnMirages.ogg', '', 0, 0, '', 1, 0, 1, '[788]', NULL, 0, 0, '[]', 100),
(25389, 'Varashta_Wish_Generic_Random', '[]', 'Your wish has been granted.', 'Audio/Dialogue/Leagues/Mirage/Varashta_Wish/Varashta_Wish_Generic_01_01.ogg', '', 0, 0, '', 10, 15000, 1, '[788]', NULL, 0, 0, '[]', 100),
